# rio

Rio is the default window system in this tree. Its goals are:

- use lib9p instead of implementing the 9p server from scratch
	-> 9p no longer in separate proc, easier synchronization
- de-couple text handling from windows
	-> text.c
- cleaner code, make it more hackable


After that had been more or less achieved some new features were implemented:

- window decorations including title bars
	- various styles:
	  - flat style (extremely minimal)
	  - simple style (TODO: maybe rename this...)
	  - windows 3.x
	  - windows 95/nt4
	- '(no)title', '(no)border' wctl messages
- support for different color schemes
	- uses named devdraw images
- virtual desktops
	- 1-2 chord on desktop opens screen menu
	- 'screenoffset' wctl message
	- '(no)sticky' wctl message
- select window with mouse by reading from `pick' file
- tabbed windows (WIP)
	- new tab: click window instead of dragging out rectangle
	- close tab: button 2 on tab
	- move tab: 1-2 and 1-3 chords
	- move tab across window: button 3 on tab or title bar,
		click new window or background
	- 'newtab' wctl message
	- 'new -id n' attach name
- Kryon-native desktop shell
	- desktop icons from /lib/q9/desktop and $home/lib/desktop
	  (label<TAB>command[<TAB>icon]); single click selects,
	  double click launches; button 3 on the desktop opens the
	  desktop context menu (the classic rio menu is on the 1-2 chord)
	- Start menu Programs/Documents lists from /lib/q9/programs
	  and $home/lib/recent
	- Run dialog with history ($home/lib/runhist)
	- Alt+Tab task switcher, Alt+F4 close, Alt+Space window menu,
	  Ctrl+Alt+Del security dialog (lock/logoff/shutdown/task
	  manager), Ctrl+Shift+Esc task manager
	- taskbar: button 3 on a task button opens the window system
	  menu, tooltips, ticking clock, double click opens a calendar
	- wctl "theme kryon:STYLE:PALETTE:MODE", "style NAME",
	  "palette NAME", "mode NAME", "wallpaper NAME", "saver MINUTES"
	- screen saver: bouncing flag after the idle timeout
- misc
	- 1-3 chord on desktop opens secondary menu

# Themes

Window decorations and the whole desktop are drawn by the system Kryon
theme engine (libkryon). At startup rio is simply itself:

	rio -theme kryon

The short option is also supported:

	rio -T kryon

Switch live through wctl:

	echo style material > /dev/wctl
	echo palette Ocean  > /dev/wctl
	echo mode dark      > /dev/wctl
	echo theme kryon:material:Ocean:dark > /dev/wctl

Styles: retro, material. Palettes: the Kryon theme catalog (Sky, Ocean,
Forest, Sunset, Lavender, Cherry, Dawn, Sage, Sepia, Default, Mint,
Cobalt, Plan9). Modes: light, dark. The q9themes control panel applet
drives all of it with a live preview.
